# Valgrind suppressions for the pyrt test suites.
#
# CPython (deps/cpython, statically linked) retains its pymalloc arena
# bookkeeping (obmalloc.c new_arena / arena_map_get) across interpreter
# finalization; after Py_EndInterpreter the arena descriptors no longer have a
# retained pointer, so valgrind classifies the arena memory as definitely or
# possibly lost. This is the documented CPython-owned class (style guide §6):
# no pyrt-owned (src/) frame is in these stacks — the only pyrt frame in any
# of them is the Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig call site inside interp boot.
#
# The two entries cover the allocator pairs valgrind observes at the top of
# those stacks: malloc→new_arena (small-object pools) and calloc→new_arena
# (arena region + arena_map). Everything below new_arena is CPython's
# interpreter initialization path (_PyGC_Init / pycore_interp_init).
{
   cpython-pymalloc-arena-malloc
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible,definite,indirect
   fun:malloc
   fun:new_arena
   ...
}
{
   cpython-pymalloc-arena-calloc
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible,definite,indirect
   fun:calloc
   fun:new_arena
   ...
}